Submitted By: Ken Moffat <ken at linuxfromscratch dot org>
Date: 2022-01-25
Initial Package Version: 5.15.2
Upstream Status: Applied
Origin: The kf5.15 branch (in git, origin/kde/5.15) - see
https://dot.kde.org/2021/04/06/announcing-kdes-qt-5-patch-collection

The kde patches are organized per-module, and include patches which
were applied to the last public 5.15.2 release, as well as unwanted
changes to force version 5.15.3 (in the case of qtscript, also 5.15.4).

These patches were checked for updates on 2022-01-25.

The following modules used by packages in BLFS have patches, for the
details of what is included, and of any patches passed over, see the
modules patches at https://rivendell.linuxfromscratch.org/~ken/qt5/
(the kf5.15-2.patch versions): qtbase, qtdeclarative, qtdoc, qtlocation,
qtmultimedia, qtquickcontrols2, qtquickcontrols, qtsvg, qttools,
qtwayland, qtwebchannel.

At this point the following modules used by packages in BLFS do not
have any useful patches: qtgraphicaleffects, qtimageformats,
qtnetworkauth, qtscript, qtsensors, qtspeech,qtx11extras, qtxmlpatterns.

QtWebEngine is not included here, we build it separately.

Those packages should be enough to provide required dependencies for
all kf5 packages, based on the details in Arch. The remaining modules
are unlikely to be used by anyone building BLFS.

